<title>NEW ZEALAND: Spectrum share consolidation approved.</title>
<headline>Spectrum share consolidation approved.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mineral exploration company Spectrum Resources Ltd on Thursday said shareholders had approved a one for 10 consolidation of ordinary shares.</p>
<p>They will get one 30 cent share for every 10 three-cent pre-consolidation shares.</p>
<p>An extraordinary general meeting also approved the issue of options for 500,000 ordinary 30 cent shares to Canaccord Capital Corporation, exercisable at 45 cents per share for up to two years. Canaccord is a Canadian broker assisting the company with its listing in Vancouver.</p>
<p>Spectrum was trading at 3.5 NZ cents.</p>
</text>
